# =============================================================================
#  .github/CODEOWNERS
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Who is automatically requested for review on which paths.
#
#  CURRENT STATE
#  This project has one maintainer, so every line below names the same person.
#  Saying so plainly is more useful than pretending a review rota exists.
#
#  WHY THE FILE IS STRUCTURED AS IF IT DID
#  Because GOVERNANCE.md section 6 says the intended growth path is DOMAIN
#  EDITORS - one person responsible for the factual accuracy of each colour
#  branch, with the maintainer responsible for the machinery and the editorial
#  standard. When that happens, this file is where it becomes real, and the
#  structure is already here waiting: replace one handle on one line and that
#  branch has an editor.
#
#  If you would like to hold a branch, say so in an issue. It is an open
#  invitation.
#
#  SYNTAX
#  Later rules win. The most specific pattern that matches a file determines
#  its owners, so the ordering below runs from general to specific.
#
#  SPDX-License-Identifier: EUPL-1.2
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Default owner for everything not matched more specifically below.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
*                                       @olaflaitinen


# =============================================================================
#  THE MACHINERY
#  Changes here affect all eighty-five records at once, so they always need
#  the maintainer regardless of who else reviews.
# =============================================================================
/src/biotechnology/core/                @olaflaitinen
/src/biotechnology/cli/                 @olaflaitinen
/src/biotechnology/__init__.py          @olaflaitinen
/tools/                                 @olaflaitinen
/tests/                                 @olaflaitinen


